  "body": "Workholding beyond the vise itself, as built-in library items, so a setup can show what really holds the part:\n- **Parallels:** a pair, with a height parameter.\n- **1-2-3 blocks and step blocks.**\n- **Strap clamps (toe clamps):** the clamp, stud and heel block, with a clamp height parameter. These matter most for collisions, because clamps sit above the part.\n- **Soft jaws:** the vise jaw replaced by a block the user can size.\n\nEach is simple original geometry with a few parameters. It's placed and checked like any fixture: one undoable command, mesh-judged.\n\nEffort: high (it feeds the collision checks).\n\n**Done means:**\n- Each item can be placed and has its parameters.\n- Strap clamps above the part are caught by the link and retract checks (#489's fixture-aware routing raises over them).\n- Pinned by tests.\n\nPart of #339.\n",
